{
  "FormatVersion": 3,
  "Id": "248675b1-7feb-5ff1-9443-53cff7da76ca"/*PhysicsNewtonsCradleExample*/,
  "Description": "A five-ball Newton's cradle: one ball is released and the opposite ball swings out.\n\nEvery ball hangs from a kinematic anchor on a ball-socket [RigidJoint]. The balls have Bounciness 1 and no friction, and are spaced with a small gap so the collisions are resolved one pair after the other.\n\nAKA: pendulum, momentum, swinging balls\n\nTips\n- A kinematic [RigidBody] is the fixed end of a joint; a static one cannot be joined.\n- LocalOffsetB of the first joint compensates for the ball starting off to the side.",
